  "lore": {
    "A": {
      "title": "What Remains of the Stair",
      "text": "A stair of metal, bent like a hair pin. Immortals once climbed it to a gate; the gate is gone. A rhyme: step on the bolts, never the plates; the plates give."
    },
    "Y": {
      "title": "Hall of Winds, Plainly",
      "text": "The wind here never stops; it pushes toward the edge. Lean into it and keep your back to a wall. A strong gust takes a person off the terrace; the Lodge lost a man that way."
    },
    "R": {
      "title": "Breath of the Cloud Court",
      "text": "They did not eat much, the immortals; they breathed. In through the nose to the count of eight, out in twelve. That is how the palace was held up; do it here and the fall slows.",
      "teaches": "cloudruins_art_2"
    },
    "G": {
      "title": "Pill Pavilion Inventory",
      "text": "Jars labeled with a single character; most are empty. A few hold dust that was once a pill. Immortals took them to live forever; they stopped when the jars ran dry."
    },
    "M": {
      "title": "The Fallen Throne",
      "text": "A throne sits at the bottom with no one in it. The legs are cut cleanly; this was not an earthquake. Someone wanted the immortal to come down, and he did."
    },
    "O": {
      "title": "Crane Terrace Marker",
      "text": "Cranes were kept here, white ones, for riding. They are gone but their nests are not; check each nest. Some hold a feather the length of your arm; worth the climb."
    },
    "U": {
      "title": "Edict of Heaven, Torn",
      "text": "The edict reads: LET NO ONE ASCEND WITHOUT BALANCE; the rest is burned. Somebody wanted to ascend without it, and tore the edict to make a point. The terraces fell soon after."
    },
    "X": {
      "title": "A Scholar's Last Page",
      "text": "I came to read the old words. I stayed to read the wind; the jade has them in its veins if you hold it to the light. There is a lot about the Accord; mostly about how little of it was kept."
    }
  },
  "riddles": {
    "?": {
      "title": "The Terrace Question",
      "question": "I have many steps but I never walk. What am I?",
